{
  "info": {
    "name": "OZ Policy Builder - MCP server (HTTP transport)",
    "description": "The nine tools of @crediolabs/policy-builder-mcp over its Streamable HTTP transport, for version 5.2.0 of the package.\n\nSTART THE SERVER FIRST:\n  npx -y @crediolabs/policy-builder-mcp@5.2.0 --http --http-port 3011\nFrom a checkout: build packages/policy-synth, then run `bun packages/policy-builder-mcp/bin/server.ts --http --http-port 3011`.\n\nThe server binds loopback only and has no authentication. It holds no key: install_policy, revoke_policy and bind_policy return unsigned transactions.\n\nThree things to know:\n\n1. The transport replies with Server-Sent Events, not plain JSON. The reply is one `data:` line holding the JSON-RPC message. The Accept header must list both application/json and text/event-stream.\n\n2. There is no session. Every POST /mcp stands alone, so requests can be sent in any order. `initialize` is included because MCP clients send it.\n\n3. The server refuses a Host or Origin that is not loopback with its port, so keep baseUrl on 127.0.0.1 or localhost with the port the server listens on.\n\nA tool refusal is a normal reply with isError true and an error envelope (code, message, retryable). A request whose name ends in \"(refusal)\" expects one.\n\nCollection variables hold testnet values: the reference account in deployments/oz-accounts.json, its rule-0 signer, the pinned interpreter and a token contract. Replace txHash with a recent testnet transaction that invokes a contract function; the RPC keeps about a week. The collection tests assert the reply shape of every request.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Protocol",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "initialize",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 0,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": {\n      \"name\": \"postman\",\n      \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "Sent because MCP clients send it. The server keeps no session, so no later request depends on it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tools/list",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/list\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "The nine tools with their descriptions and input schemas."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Read-only",
      "description": "Answers without a key and without building a transaction. Only record_transaction, the simulate and verify checks and get_interpreter_info with verifyLive read the network.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "get_interpreter_info",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"get_interpreter_info\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"network\": \"{{network}}\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mcp"]
            },
            "description": "The pinned interpreter, its limits and the ceilings. No network call."
          }
        },
